 268:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @brief    Extended Peripheral Control functions
 269:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *
 270:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** @verbatim
 271:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
 272:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                       ##### Peripheral Control functions #####
 273:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
 274:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This section provides the following functions:
 275:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_MultiProcessorEx_AddressLength_Set() API optionally sets the UART node address
 276:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          detection length to more than 4 bits for multiprocessor address mark wake up.
 277:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_StopModeWakeUpSourceConfig() API defines the wake-up from stop mode
 278:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          trigger: address match, Start Bit detection or RXNE bit status.
 279:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_EnableStopMode() API enables the UART to wake up the MCU from stop mode
 280:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_DisableStopMode() API disables the above functionality
 281:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 282:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This subsection also provides a set of additional functions providing enhanced reception
 283:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     services to user. (For example, these functions allow application to handle use cases
 284:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     where number of data to be received is unknown).
 285:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 286:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Compared to standard reception services which only consider number of received
 287:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         data elements as reception completion criteria, these functions also consider additional ev
 288:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         as triggers for updating reception status to caller :
 289:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection of inactivity period (RX line has not been active for a given period).
 290:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by IDLE event, i.e. RX line has been in idle state (normally 
 291:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for 1 frame time, after last received byte.
 292:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by RTO, i.e. line has been in idle state
 293:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for a programmable time, after last received byte.
 294:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection that a specific character has been received.
 295:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 296:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
 297:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The reception is performed in polling mode, until either expected number 
 298:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            or till IDLE event occurs. Reception is handled only during function execution.
 299:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            When function exits, no data reception could occur. HAL status and number of actually re
 300:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            are returned by function after finishing transfer.
 301:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The reception is performed using Interrupts or DMA.
 302:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            These API's return the HAL status.
 303:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 304:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when using DMA mode.
 305:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback() user callback will be executed during Receive process
 306:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a reception error is det
 307:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 308:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Blocking mode API:
 309:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle()
 310:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 311:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with Interrupt:
 312:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle_IT()
 313:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 314:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with DMA:
 315:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle_DMA()
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccUga7Nf.s 			page 7


